# Response Identity Footer

## MANDATORY — CANNOT BE SKIPPED

Every single response to the user MUST end with an `Agent Info` section.
This includes short confirmations, one-line answers, and error messages.
There are NO exceptions.

## Required Fields (in this exact order)

1. `Agent Name`
2. `Model`
3. `Version`

## Rules

- Place this section at the **very end** of the response, after all other content.
- Use concise one-line values.
- If a value is unavailable, write `unknown` — never omit the field.
- Use this exact format (no deviations):

```
---
Agent Info
- Agent Name: Cursor Assistant
- Model: claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking
- Version: unknown
```

## Checklist Before Submitting Any Response

- [ ] Have I written the `---` divider?
- [ ] Have I written `Agent Info`?
- [ ] Have I listed Agent Name, Model, and Version?
- [ ] Is this section the absolute last thing in my response?
